<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shashe River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Shashe is a river of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> that rises in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a> and forms part of the border between Botswana and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a> before joining the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limpopo">Limpopo</a>. The confluence, where Botswana, Zimbabwe and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> meet, was the heart of the Mapungubwe kingdom in the 11th to 13th centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shashe-river.jpg" alt="Shashe River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Babakathy at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shashe_at_SIS.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
